From 44570143def994ce5cb5cfa0502ab748f3ae0f2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel <2660793+imDaniel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:43:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Project target attention writers with graph-safe row controls

Base: r6v plus V2 steering control data. Rationale: explicit projection before mHC, preserving the existing rank-order BF16 boundary, and bounded preallocated scratch. Quality: zero dose skips single-writer stores; draft layers have no bound profile. Register aligned and SP-sliced controls before warmup freeze. Validation: 69 CPU tests passed; 21 synthetic GPU cases added but not yet run; TP4, graphs, output quality and performance remain unqualified. Upstream status: independent downstream experiment; no upstream submission.
